---
source: crates/wolf_sema/tests/typecheck_diagnostics.rs
expression: "render_types(&[(&[], \"main.lu\", src)])"
---
error[E0409]: `.starts_with(…)` cannot be applied to `str ! {none}`
  --> mem:///main.lu:10:8
   |
10 |     if rest.starts_with("4") {
   |        ^^^^ this is `str ! {none}`
   |
   = note: a `!T` is two values, never one, and no operator reads it ([type.row.operand]): a member
     read and a method call read their base as an operator reads its operand, and `?`, `else`
     and `match` are the whole of how a row is handled. Handle it first —
     `rest?.starts_with(…)`, `(rest else "").starts_with(…)` — and read what it yields.
